 "findings": [
  {
   "date": "2026-11-21",
   "topic": "low point",
   "text": "LowPointDistance IS reported in the TrackMan export. An earlier note in this project said it was not. 17 Nov driver median -98 mm (behind the ball, correct for driver). 17 Nov 7-iron median +58 mm, range +16 to +128 (ahead of the ball, healthy). So the 7-iron low-on-face strikes are NOT caused by a low point at or behind the ball. Cause still unknown. Track lowPointMm at every checkpoint."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-11-21",
   "topic": "two separate faults",
   "text": "The open face is present from the first ball and does not change across a session. The out-to-in path builds as the session goes on. Treat them as separate problems: face is technique, path is fatigue or compensation."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-11-21",
   "topic": "impact offset geometry correction",
   "text": "Reaching or standing too far, then retracting, predicts TOE contact. Heel contact goes with the club moving away from the body. An earlier note had this backwards. The direction offset will move when arm hang is corrected is therefore not predictable; track the median and follow it."
  }
 ],
